     "kind": "debate",
     "text": "The verb וְנִבְרְכ֣וּ is verb, niphal (hence simple, passive), consecutive perfect (hence future/present, indicative), third person, either gender, plural. This stem can be passive (\"will be blessed\") or reflexive (\"will bless themselves\", that is, use Abram's name in blessing). The Septuagint εὐλογηθήσονται and the Vulgate benedicentur are both passive, as are the English versions here.",
